this video contains spoilers for better  call saul through season 6 episode 5. if  you're interested in this great  character who only really has one  problem but you haven't watched that far  yet then this isn't the video you're  looking for  there was a point in season four a  better call saw where if i'm being  honest i struggled to care what was  going on with the story about gus  building his super lab i knew it would  eventually get completed i knew that gus  and mike would both survive the series  and i knew that none of the germans  involved would play a significant role  in breaking bad more than that it felt  like the whole cartel side of the story  needed something to make it feel vital  because it was drifting away from the  main story about jimmy mcgill sure mike  needed to continue his descent to become  the guy we knew him to be in the  original series but the writers had the  problem of working against the nature of  the show since it's a prequel they met  this challenge by introducing a new  character from the salamanca family that  pesky brood of characters who all sort  of have that person you hope you never  find yourself mixed up with temperament  about them eduardo salamanca aka lalo  was a nephew of hector that was  previously unknown and a cousin to tuco  marco and leonel his name was first  mentioned in that much-discussed  throwaway line in the desert from saul  goodman's first episode that also gave  us nacho jimmy's fear there hinted that  their paths would eventually cross and  that he must be a pretty imposing  character to still be on his mind 4  years later that is not terribly  surprising the salamancas all have that  going for them they manage to be great  antagonists despite the fact that  they're a bit one-dimensional with that  one dimension being they're unstable and  potentially violent it was clear from  his very first scene that lalo stood out  from the other members in that regard  when nacho found him cooking in the  kitchen of the restaurant the family  runs their drug business out of i didn't  know he was related until he said it out  loud he was cooking like we'd seen tuko  do before but it came off as the type of  guy you wanted to get to know better  rather than generally making your skin  crawl of course in the next episode he  cleared up any confusion that he might  just be a black sheep when he murdered  an absolutely innocent clerk at travel  travelwire while following mike he  exposed himself as a cold-blooded killer  leaving no room for debate the show  knows how captivating tony dalton can be  in this role and seem to balance that  out by having him periodically do  something that reminds us of his  brutality in case we might forget it's  part of what makes it work he's  fascinating because of this capacity to  be more than one thing at the same time  it's the perfect mixture of charm and  menace that makes you warm up to him in  every scene while fearing what he might  do next he's absolutely dastardly but  has a few redeeming things mixed in  there to keep it interesting he appeared  to care about the people at his compound  and even though he didn't have a problem  killing his body double matteo the look  on his face before that happened  indicated that he didn't enjoy it  although there wasn't much to say he had  remorse beyond that and the scene where  he noticed the family of fred from  travelwire in the courtroom without  skipping a beat seems to back that up he  breathed life back into the cartel side  of things by being a worthy adversary  for gus and by hiring jimmy as his  lawyer he solved the problem of the two  different stories drifting apart he  matches up well with both of these  characters gus isn't able to outmaneuver  him and jimmy isn't able to out talk him  he's a nearly perfect character that  even this late in the story integrates  seamlessly he's a fan favorite that only  seems to get better and the only problem  there is is that lalo salamanca must die  i say must because i don't see any way  around it he has to go down and it has  to happen before the end of this season  of course it's always possible that the  show could swerve hard into new  territory but even then something fairly  contrived would have to happen i mean  could lola get hit on the head in  germany and wake up with amnesia in the  hospital under an assumed identity  technically yes but that doesn't feel  like the show we've been watching plus  they've been leaning in hard to the  effect that his being out there in the  world is having on gus the chicken man  who is usually composed and calculated  is currently falling apart so how would  you explain his getting it together if  this threat were still out there i've  seen a lot of comments asking if he can  make it out of the series alive could he  show up in the gene timeline could he  just generally outlive everyone but i  don't really see a path to that i think  some of this comes from the fact that  jimmy was still afraid of him in that  scene in the desert the counter-argument  to that is what gus says to hector when  he goes to gloat about killing the  cartel during the breaking bad timeline  he tells him that jesse killed the only  other salamanca who was left alive his  grandson joaquin and says that the  salamanca name will die with hector  which basically completes his revenge  arc and he looks absolutely certain that  it's the truth the gus and better call  saul season 6 wouldn't be able to make  that claim also none of the cartel stuff  from the original series makes sense if  lalo is still out there somewhere bolsa  and eladio would have to still think  he's dead and hector would just have to  be there not knowing what happened to  him after he found out he was alive with  his ending nacho provided cover for  everything to make sense as long as lalo  doesn't re-emerge he's already faked his  death once and gus didn't actually  believe it and things seem to be setting  up for a final confrontation which we  know he can't win so in my mind the  question is not if lalo will die it's  when i suppose if you wanted to nitpick  the character he can be borderline  superhero-ish and that is something that  pops up every now and again when he  escapes out a two-story window or  something along those lines but in light  of the situation that sort of works in  the favor of the upcoming conclusion in  order to defeat him gus will have to  outdo himself and that should make for a  memorable ending there's also the  possibility that he could bring more  about mr frink to light in the process  and that means he could have a lasting  influence on the story after he's gone  lalo is dashing he's dynamic he's been a  great addition to this late part of the  series and he's gonna have to get out of  the way so the story can move on and i  think that is a good place to leave  things let me know in the comments how  you think his story might end right now  it all feels like it's heading towards a  showdown in the super lab but do you  think there's room for a twist does  nachos ending playing out exactly how it  should have make you suspicious do you  think that they'll go a different  direction here or do you think it's just  going to be a fascinating showdown where  one menacing character out does the  other please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon
 

